<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  OWNER HOTFIX (2026-09-19) — keep the notification small icon in release.

  `ic_nt_notification` is referenced ONLY from Dart, as the runtime resource NAME
  the notification plugin resolves through
  `Resources.getIdentifier(name, "drawable", packageName)`:

    * `AndroidInitializationSettings('@drawable/ic_nt_notification')` registers the
      default icon for every notification, and
    * `AndroidNotificationDetails(icon: 'ic_nt_notification')` names it per send.

  Nothing in the Android build references it, so the release resource shrinker
  (AGP 9.0.1 enables it for release) removed it from the shipped bundle.  With the
  drawable absent the plugin's initialization fails its drawable check, the default
  icon is never persisted, and every reminder alarm then crashes the process inside
  `FlutterLocalNotificationsPlugin.setSmallIcon`, because the fallback path unboxes a
  null `iconResourceId`.  The reminder never appears and the app disappears from the
  foreground — the reported "app closes itself at the reminder time".  `tools:keep` is the documented AGP mechanism for a resource that is only
  resolved by name at runtime.  It keeps exactly this one drawable; nothing else
  changes.

  OWNER DECISION (2026-09-22, final) — the notification LARGE icon was removed
  again, so `@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground` is NOT resolved by name at
  runtime any more and is deliberately not listed here: its only remaining
  reference is the adaptive launcher icon in the Android resources themselves,
  which the shrinker already honours.  This list keeps exactly the one drawable
  that is still named from Dart.  It now lists BOTH names this app resolves at
  runtime: the canonical app-icon resource that carries the notification identity
  today (`@mipmap/ic_launcher`, which the plugin's own documentation tells you to
  keep here when it is used as the notification icon) and the Android-compliant
  monochrome mark that remains the documented one-constant revert.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@drawable/ic_nt_notification,@mipmap/ic_launcher" />
